# Agent skills & local specs (local only — never pushed to GitHub)
#
# NOTE: .uihub-agent/ is listed below at owner request, BUT its 142 existing
# files are STILL TRACKED and still pushed. .gitignore has no effect on files
# already in the index, so that entry only prevents NEW files under
# .uihub-agent/ from being added — it does NOT untrack anything.
#
# The knowledge base stays in the repo because 5 CI jobs (security-scan,
# knowledge, config-drift, intelligence, task-routing in
# .github/workflows/ci.yml) and 19 root package.json scripts execute from it.
# security-scan is a `needs:` gate on most other jobs, so removing the files
# fails the whole pipeline. To truly untrack it you must BOTH run
# `git rm -r --cached .uihub-agent` AND remove those CI jobs and scripts.
# Do not rely on this line alone.
#
# NOTE: .github/ is intentionally NOT ignored. CI workflows are project
# configuration: an untracked workflow means every agent reads a CI definition
# that does not exist for anyone else, and the pipeline cannot be reviewed in a
# pull request. Removed in Phase 6 (agent.md 6.9/6.10).
#
# .agents/, .claude/ and .opencode/ remain ignored. They hold personal local
# tooling and skills, not shared project contracts. Confirmed by owner in Phase 6.
.agents/
.opencode/
.claude/
.uihub-agent/
component-specs/

